Rajiv,

Are you logging blocked connections with your firewall? If so are there any
hints in /var/log/messages about the conntections being refused?

Maybe in.talkd needs to be used in conjunction with the tcp wrapper daemon?
like this:

service talk
{
        disable                 = no
        socket_type             = dgram
        wait                    = no
        user                    = nobody
        group                   = tty
        server                  = /usr/sbin/tcpd
        server_args             = /usr/sbin/in.talkd
}


On a system I have at home (based on 6.2) I have this:

service talk
{
        flags       = REUSE NAMEINARGS
        socket_type = dgram
        protocol    = udp
        wait        = yes
        user        = nobody
        group       = tty
        server      = /usr/sbin/tcpd
        server_args = in.talkd
}


This was generated by the xconv.pl script.

Hope this helps.

Collin




