I just got a Digital Server 5305, and I'm learning the hard way that a lot
of video cards don't work in it.

I'm looking for a card that has enough RAM to do 1280x1024 in TrueColor.
Something that supports multihead configurations would be nice.  Mostly it
needs to be supported as the primary display to be initialized by the SRM
console (I have the latest firmware release V6.0-4).  Framebuffer support
in the kernel would also be nice so I could get a few extra rows and
columns of text on the Linux console.  I'd also like some OpenGL support
in X, but that is low on my list.

I'm told that Permedia 2 based card will work.  But they seem kinda short
on RAM these days.  The Permedia 3s look better, but the person I was
talking to wasn't sure about SRM support.

What really caught my eye as I was looking around was a GLINT R3 based
card, the 3DLabs Oxygen VX1.  Is it known to work with the SRM console of
the DS5305?  I don't see a console driver, does SVGATextMode work on the
Alpha?

Thanks a lot,
Chris
