On Tue, Apr 02, 2002 at 02:41:31PM -0500, Chris Meadors wrote:
>
> I just got a Digital Server 5305, and I'm learning the hard way that a lot
> of video cards don't work in it.

OK; whitebox 5305 == bluebox AS1200 == "tincup" aka "baby rawhide"

> I'm looking for a card that has enough RAM to do 1280x1024 in TrueColor.
> Something that supports multihead configurations would be nice.  Mostly it
> needs to be supported as the primary display to be initialized by the SRM
> console (I have the latest firmware release V6.0-4).  Framebuffer support
> in the kernel would also be nice so I could get a few extra rows and
> columns of text on the Linux console.  I'd also like some OpenGL support
> in X, but that is low on my list.
>
> I'm told that Permedia 2 based card will work.  But they seem kinda short
> on RAM these days.  The Permedia 3s look better, but the person I was
> talking to wasn't sure about SRM support.

1280x1024x4 means you need something with 8MB, unless the card/driver
can do packed 24-bit pixels. Only one I know that can is the Matrox
Millennium I and II (perhaps later ones as well), and they are old
and you'd need the add-on memory board (rare).

Permedia-2 cards typically have the 8MB, but at 24-bit depth have
poor RAMDAC performance and won't do a reasonable refresh rate like
75Hz. They *do* allow multihead, if you can find one that has the
VGA-disable switch/jumper.

Neither Millenniums nor Permedias have had OpenGL support under
Linux on Alpha; for that you'd need something like a 3DFx Voodoo-3
card, which may not work with the SRM BIOS emulator. Other cards
that'll do OpenGL on Alpha (ATI Rage128 and Radeon) are notoriously
hard on BIOS emulators and don't work on most older boxes.

> What really caught my eye as I was looking around was a GLINT R3 based
> card, the 3DLabs Oxygen VX1.  Is it known to work with the SRM console of
> the DS5305?  I don't see a console driver, does SVGATextMode work on the
> Alpha?

Permedia-3 cards (eg Oxygen VX1) have 32MB and good RAMDAC
performance.  They've also tended to be more reliable than some other
recent cards WRT working with the BIOS emulators in the SRM of older
Alphas. Support under XFree86 4.1.0 and later is good. Multihead is
not supported on them with older boxes because they have no jumper,
though it does work on the EV6 boxen because of console tweaks.

I've got access to a bluebox AS1200, and I'll see if I can try some
of the cards I have in it tomorrow (Wednesday), and will let you
know what I find...

--Jay++

