With regards to your message at 05:23 PM 4/3/02, John Weez. Where you stated:
>Hello all,
>
>  I have purchased a new fan for my alpha 164lx motherboard and  when i 
> put in the new fan it does not activate. Yes..it is plugged in 
> tothemotherboard and my old fan works.
>
>  I do notice that the colored power wires are in a differrent order than 
> the power wires on my current cpu fan.. If I were to cut the wires on my 
> new fan and attach a new power connector with the wires in the same order 
> as my old fan, would this in theory make the new fan work??


The Alpha boards do not use the same pinout on the connector as PC boards.
Please correct the connector by moving the pins to the right places.
Failure to do so will likely damage t4he fan, motherboard, power supply, or 
all.

If unsure which pin goes where the motherboard connector may be checked 
with a meter.
On most fans the 12V lead is red, the ground is black, and the yellow is 
for tach pulse for speed monitoring.

Most Alphas will not start without the fan hooked up correctly.

Hope this helps!


