On Wednesday 03 April 2002 23:34, you wrote:
> I would like to be able to restore an Alpha system running RedHat 7.1,
> Linux version 2.4.3-12smp, using a remote tape drive.  I was able
> to get into Rescue mode from the Jumpstart V1.4 CD.  However I got the
> message "eth0: unknown interface" when I tried to ifconfig eth0.
>
> Does anyone know if its possible to get the system to recognize eth0 in
> rescue mode or know another method for restoring from a remote tape
> drive.  If I have to build a new rescue CD, I would appreciate instructions
> as I haven't done this before. This system uses the SRM cosole and aboot to
> boot.
Hi,
as far as I know, you have to install the appropriate network-card driver 
from the commandline. So, something like
modprobe ne2k-pci
could do the trick. Of course, you should know what card is installed, and 
what the driver is called like. I can't say for sure, but perhaps the
lspci
command is also on the rescue-CD, like this you'd see what your network card 
is.

Greets

ineiti




