> a ES40 and a DS10, we could have a kernel that runs on both (when multiple 
> CPUs are installed).  
> 
> On our single ES40, I found the SMP kernel failed as well, but turning off
> SMP allowed the kernel to boot.
> 
> Thanks for the clues that various people gave around the place.  Does anyone
> know of any tuning guides for a DS10 with 1 GB RAM, and an ES40 with 4 GB
> RAM and 340 GB of disk (in a RA3000) - don't ask, the hardware was bought 
> before there was any IT staff :(.

Try this patch and see if it helps on the ES40 when booting an SMP
kernel.  I think gcc is spitting out bad code for one of the functions,
but the function is unnecessary in 2.4 anyway (patch attached).

C

