On Tue, Apr 02, 2002 at 04:34:13PM -0800, Stephen Williams wrote:
> 
> Jay.Estabrook@compaq.com said:
> > Permedia-3 cards (eg Oxygen VX1) have 32MB and good RAMDAC
> > performance.  They've also tended to be more reliable than some other
> > recent cards WRT working with the BIOS emulators in the SRM of older
> > Alphas. Support under XFree86 4.1.0 and later is good.
> 
> Does "good XFree86 4.1.0 support" include sparse mapping machines
> such as the PC164?

Apparently not for AS1200 (I'll try to do the same for PC164 soon)... :-(

Here's what I found yesterday on an AS1200 (bluebox) with SRM version 6.0
and BIOS emulator X3.00, and a 2.4.9-based kernel, and XFree86 4.1.0:

card		console		XFree86		Notes
====		=======		=======		=====

Permedia-2	yes		yes		ELSA Gloria Synergy 8MB
Permedia-3	yes		no*		VX1, X crashed during start
ATI R128	no		no		Rage128, BIOSem hang
ATI Radeon	no		no		32MB SDR, BIOSem hang
ATI RV200	no		no		7500, BIOSem hang
Voodoo3		no		no		3000, no hang but no video
Savage4		yes		no+		Stealth III S540, no X driver
TNT2		no		no		no hang but no video
S3Virge		yes		no*		X SPARSE mapping problem

* == might be fixable
+ == may work if the driver is built

So, not a very good track record... :-(

I'd like to take a look at the VX1 and S3Virge problems, but I don't
know when or even if I'll get a chance in the near future. It *is*
possible that these problems are fixed in XFree86 4.2.0, which would
be worth a try.

I believe that SRM console V6.0-4 is the latest available for AS1200,
so there's none newer that might have improved BIOS emulation, which
is the biggest problem found above.

BTW, I didn't try TGA or TGA2, but I assume that they'll work... ;-}

Good luck.

--Jay++

