Once I booted from the jumpstart CD and got in rescue mode, I found the
driver in /lib/modules/2.2.16cpq/net/3c59x.o. I tried modprobe -v 3c59x but
the prompt came
right back and eth0 didn't show up. I then tried modprobe -V, lsmod, insmod
but the prompt comes right back with no output.

The driver shows up under the modinfo command 

/sbin/modinfo -d 3c59x
3COM 3c590/3c900 Series Vortex/Boomerang driver

I'm new to Linux so I'm not sure whats going on.  

I followed a suggestion from Michal Jaegermann to boot the system from a
Red Hat installation, pretend that you want to "update" it and switch to a
text console with Alt-F2 (or Ctrl-Alt-F2).  That got me into a shell and
all I had to do
was ifconfig eth0 and I was on the network. 

Even though my problem is solved, I would still like to know why the modprobe
command didn't work if anyone has any clues.

Thanks for your help.

Marci






