"Robert M. Riches Jr." <richesr1@inetarena.com> wrote:
> Did the 0.9.9 source mentioned above include Redhat patches,
> or was it non-patched?

The 0.9.9 sources I origially referred to were from
mozilla-0.9.9-0.src.rpm from mozilla.org.  It appears to have been
packaged by Red Hat (rpm says the build host was
tooth.toronto.redhat.com).  It has a pile of patches in it already.

But wait...

Relative to the current rawhide (0.9.9-5), 0.9.9-0 is missing an
important patch for alpha, apparently.  From the spec file:

* Tue Mar 14 2002 Christopher Blizzard <blizzard@redhat.com>
- Add patch that fixes crash with some images on 64 bit machines, like
  the alpha

The patch (mozilla-0.9.9-64bitimage.patch) has a fix for
nsImageGTK::DrawToImage().  This is the routine 0.9.9-0 crashes in
all the time.

So now I'm building 0.9.9-5 :-)

Cheers,
Craig




