On Thu, Apr 04, 2002 at 06:03:40PM -0500, Peter Petrakis wrote:
>  
> > Seriously, though, both Millennium I and II do usually work, but they
> > are VERY hard to find these days, which is why I didn't mention them.
> 
> I found quite a few on ebay. real cheap too. 

If you can find the ones with the additional memory expansion, you can
get a Mill I up to 8MB and a Mill II up to 16MB, I believe.

> > Savage4 ought to work well in 2D on UP1000, and they are most likely
> > quite reasonable (mine is a Diamond Stealth III S540 PCI).
> 
> I think thats the same one I have. 32MB? 

Yup.

> I suppose that makes the best 2D/3D card for the 1K the Matrox
> G200/400. 

You may require the AGP version; I dunno if the G200 or G400 PCI
versions can be made to do 3D. The ATI Rage128 and Radeon PCI cards
have GART-like hardware assist that make it reasonable (PCI bus is
33MHz, AGP is at least 66MHz, IIRC).

The Matrox cards don't have this particular assist, but I seem to
remember some talk on some mailing-list about trying to fake the PCI
card into believing it is AGP and perform the GART-like mapping using
the Alpha scatter/gather DMA window support, but I don't remember any
details.

--Jay++

