Chris,
I am not sure what a DS5305 looks like but I have an
"ELSA Gloria L" with the DELTA and 500TX chips in
a PWS500 and the SRM console works and when the XFree 4.2
'glint' driver takes over you get "X" and the virtual consoles
work fine. OpenGL works (software rendering) so 'glxgears' runs.
I am running RedHat 7.1 and KDE. I am not
sure I would call it "good" - it is slower than YDL on my
Mac G4 with Rage 128 but it all works and I have seen
Gloria-L boards on ebay for $10-$30. Hope this helps,
It has 8meg+8meg RAM and dot clock up to 220MHz so
1280x1024 should be OK - tho my monitor won't do that.
Stephen Lewis


