I run FreeBSD on a PWS 500au and, while not trying to be disrespectful in
any way, shape or form, find it runs very, very nicely.  I tried several
Linux distro's on it .... RH was ok, but since I'm used to Debian, tried
that - couldn't get it to get past the installer.  Tried FreeBSD - and it
just *works*.

The ports (optional packages outside the base OS) system rocks too!

Cheers,
Rob




