Hello to everybody

I am new to this list and I have a problem. We have two UP1000 (21264) 
with a board from API running RedHat 5.2. They have the AlphaBios 
version 5.7-11, I think. I want to upgrade to RedHat 7.1 and I am not 
able. I did the following:

1) Made 2 floppies with the generic and ramdisk images from the RedHat 
CDROM.

2) Copied the kernel in the CDROM into the DOS partition.

3) Run the APB utility from the DOS partition and issue the command

apb> bootl up1000.pal vmlinux.gz root=/dev/fd0 load_ramdisk=1


The computer halts before anything comes in the screen. This procedure 
works for RedHat 6.2 but, as I am upgrading, I wanted to go all the way 
to RedHat 7.1. The difference between RedHat's 6.2 and 7.1 is that the 
former has a root file system on the RedHat CD, so that I could boot 
with (hdc=myCDROM)

apb> bootl up1000.pal vmlinux.gz root=/dev/hdc


Looking in the mailing list I tried other things that did not work:

1) I could not change to SRM. There is no option for that on the 
AlphaBios of the UP1000.

2) I did not try MILO because I did not find the name of my machine on 
the systems that support MILO. Can I use another?


Does any one have any idea that could help?


Thanks in advance


Jorge Romao

