7.1 has a 2.4 kernel I think, and I doubt it has legacy start address set, 
and apb was never updated for this. You could try using the kernel floppy 
from a previous version (like 6.2 or 7.0) with the ramdisk floppy from 
7.1. 
 
> apb> bootl up1000.pal vmlinux.gz root=/dev/hdc
> 
> Looking in the mailing list I tried other things that did not work:
> 
> 1) I could not change to SRM. There is no option for that on the 
> AlphaBios of the UP1000.

Yes you can. Get the package from here:
http://www.api-networks.com/products/downloads/customer_support/UP1000/up1000_srm_5.6_beta.zip

Unzip that and read the directions inside.

> 2) I did not try MILO because I did not find the name of my machine on 
> the systems that support MILO. Can I use another?

There is no MILO for Nautilus systems.

