Dear Rich Payne

Thank you for your e-mail. I have tried your suggestions and I have a 
few points.


> 
> 7.1 has a 2.4 kernel I think, and I doubt it has legacy start address set, 
> and apb was never updated for this. You could try using the kernel floppy 
> from a previous version (like 6.2 or 7.0) with the ramdisk floppy from 
> 7.1. 
>  
> 


I tried this. I got to the point where the installation program starts, 
but it did not recognize the CDROM. I also tried NFS and Hard Disk 
install without success. The software was not recognized.




>>
>>1) I could not change to SRM. There is no option for that on the 
>>AlphaBios of the UP1000.
>>
> 
> Yes you can. Get the package from here:
> http://www.api-networks.com/products/downloads/customer_support/UP1000/up1000_srm_5.6_beta.zip
> 
> Unzip that and read the directions inside.



I got the package and read the instructions. They seem clear. However if 
I look at the UP1000 manual the jumper setting (J43=on) is not 
documented. What is there is

J42=on, J43=off  -> restores factory defaults
J42=on, J43=on   -> Reload ADE (which I do not know waht it is)

There is no setting like (J42=off, J43=on) documented as upgrading the 
firmware. But perhaps it is OK.

The other thing is that I also got the nautilus.rom in case things go 
wrong. But I do not have the instructions to reload it and restore the 
machine to its original state.


Any comment?


Thanks for the help.

Regards

Jorge Romao




