> 
> I got the package and read the instructions. They seem clear. However if 
> I look at the UP1000 manual the jumper setting (J43=on) is not 
> documented. What is there is
> 
> J42=on, J43=off  -> restores factory defaults
> J42=on, J43=on   -> Reload ADE (which I do not know waht it is)

ADE = Alpha Diagnostic Environment (if my memory is right). It's a piece 
of console firmware that was unique to API boards. It allows you to run 
some basic tests on the boards and manipulate the firmware. The jumper you 
set involkes ADE at the firmware maintenance entry point.
 
> There is no setting like (J42=off, J43=on) documented as upgrading the 
> firmware. But perhaps it is OK.
> 
> The other thing is that I also got the nautilus.rom in case things go 
> wrong. But I do not have the instructions to reload it and restore the 
> machine to its original state.

The package you downloaded has 3 parts, and if I remember correctly 
there are 2 ADE images and SRM Console (they all have part numbers, 
something like 6100043.rom etc...). The upgrade to SRM involves flashing 
those three images into flash, overwriting the old AlphaBIOS. If you need 
to go back to AlphaBIOS again then you would just overwrite the SRM 
console image with the nautilus.rom image. Once you're inside the ADE 
firmware screen it will show you which image is where.

--rdp


