From: "Peter Watkinson" <peterw871@netscapeonline.co.uk>
Subject: Wireless networking

I don't know about anyone's that work with Linux in general, all my Linux
boxes are connected directly.
> How much are they likely to cost?

I bought mine for about $125 US each. The router/gateway cost me about
$400US.

> How about hubs do they need to be compatible?

All you need to pay attention to on that is whether or not it uses the same
wireless protocol. The most common to find (and the one I use) is 802.11b.

> How far are their range?

I can see a second router that I've located at about 1000 feet from me, and
I'm looking from inside a groundfloor apartment in the middle of San Jose,
so it's not exactly an ideal situation.

If you can find the drivers I've had a great deal of success with the
Linksys WMP11 PCI card, and the Linksys Etherfast Wireless Accesspoint +
Cable/DSL with 4-port switch. I will also take this opportunity to strongly
suggest that you change the encryption key, I've found that simply by doing
that you eliminate all unauthorized accesses. From a security standpoint
it's not a good solution, but it seems to be realistically effective.
                    Joe




