> From: Peter Watkinson [mailto:peterw871@netscapeonline.co.uk]

> I don't know to much about wireless networking. Are there any wireless
> networking cards that work with Alpha Linux? How much are 
> they likely to
> cost?  Do they work with regular x86 linux? How about hubs do 
> they need to
> be compatible? How far are their range?

I've been using a Multia with a Compaq WL-110 PCcard as my "hub". It's not entirely obvious (well it wasn't to me at the time) but you don't need to buy a fancy wireless hub. If you've only got two systems that you want to connect wirelessly, just buy two cards and set up an "Ad-hoc" network. In my case, I have three systems in an Ad-Hoc arrangement - it works fine (well mostly - see below).

My network has the Multia running Linux/AXP, a W2K laptop and an iPAQ running Linux.

I have had some problems with the network - under reasonable load it all works fine but if I try to use VNC on my laptop to talk to my W2K workstation which is attached to the wired network via the Multia I can expect the wireless network to collapse and until I upgraded to 2.2.20 the Multia would be also be completely unresponsive.

If it wasn't such a pain I'd upgrade to 2.4.x to see if it fixes the problem.

