You can read all about VNC at:

	http://www.uk.research.att.com/vnc/

Basically VNC is an operating system neutral "PC Anywhere" tool. There is a port of VNC to Linux/Alpha (so that at least there's a little on-topic content here).

An iPAQ can be extended with a sleeve that allows you to add a PCcard. I use a standard Compaq WL-110 card to give wireless connectivity. Information on iPAQ is at:

	http://www.compaq.com/showroom/handhelds.html

Information on the WL-110 is:

	http://www.compaq.com/products/wireless/wlan/

Compaq help sponsor the port of Linux to the iPAQ. More information from:

	http://www.handhelds.org and http://intimate.handhelds.org/

Hope this helps.

