On Thursday 11 April 2002 11:22 am, Peter Watkinson wrote:
> Thanks Huw,
>
> What is VNC? Also can you connect an Ipaq to a wireless network? Does it
> require a special wireless network card? How did you install Linux on the
> Ipaq?

1) VNC is a remote graphic display protocol, similar in some ways to X or 
Citrix's ICA. It's GPL'd and runs on just about any platform you care to 
think of, including Linux/Alpha (it used to segfault like mad, but it's 
finally been made 64-bit clean).

2) You can get the ipaq going wireless, but you need buy a number of addons 
(including a different back IIRC). If you want to install Linux on it I'd 
recommend looking at handhelds.org, which has all the information you need.

cheers
john




