----- Original Message -----
From: "Davies, Huw" <Huw.Davies@Compaq.com>
> I have had some problems with the network - under reasonable load it all
works fine but if I try to use VNC on my laptop to talk to my W2K
workstation which is attached to the wired network via the Multia I can
expect the wireless network to collapse and until I upgraded to 2.2.20 the
Multia would be also be completely unresponsive.

I can actually tell you why. It's actually not that the network has become
loaded that is the problem. The problem is that with most (if not all)
current 802.11b cards, the card needs help from the system, when you load
down your cpu doing intense work, you'll actually find that your network
goes down. It should be possible to correct this by changing the priority of
all the running executables to give the driver more room to play.
                    Joe




