I have a Xircom Rex Pro-5000 which I use as my appointment and contact keeper (A really next idea - pity Intel took them over and killed it. See http://support.intel.com/support/peripherals/xc/pda/) so my iPAQ is a play toy and a reward from me to me for completing a big project early!

Basically I just use it as a wireless web pad - it's neat to have instant on web access when sitting in front of the TV (so many channels, so much rubbish :-). I sometimes play MP3s as well - I have a nice MP3 server sitting on my network. At one stage I did have fantasies of writing code, but there doesn't appear to be enough hours in the day.

I guess you could say it's a replacement for my Newton.

