OK, my quick wireless on Multia HOW-TO :-)

I have a standard RedHat 6.2 installation.

This has been updated to kernel 2.2.20. Note that there's a small patch required to get 2.2.20 to compile on Alpha. I understand this problem is resolved in 2.2.21.

I have also installed PCcard services (pcmcia-cs-3.1.32) which compiles out of the box and supports the Compaq WL-110 wireless card (along with lots of others).

After that it's a simple matter of configuring the wireless card. There are configuration files that can be changed but I just wrote a simple three line script executed at the end of startup that sets up appropriate ipchains rules, configures the ip address of the card - it appears as eth2 in my configuration (eth0 is the cable modem, eth1 is my home wired network) and finally uses iwconfig to set the ESSID and MODE of the wireless. One day I should add encryption too....

Hope that helps.

