From: Ben Collins <bcollins@debian.org>

That's only because the alpha folks have not tested, nor enabled the
config options. They should work for you (atleast, I think the ohci394
driver will, along with sbp2). To enable the config option, edit
arch/alpha/config.in and add this (next to a compatable line, e.g. one
that starts with "source").

source drivers/ieee1394/Config.in

---

Here you go. Hope it works for you as well. If it does let us know and
I'll go and join that lkml list and go bother the alpha maintainer.

Felix

