On Sun, Apr 14, 2002 at 06:04:29PM -0600, Chris Price wrote:
> 
> 	I've got my PC164 booting from IDE (no small chore the first time). I
> installed Redhat 7.0, and proceeded to attempt to upgrade to
> kernel 2.4.18.
> 
> 	Compile, install, modify aboot.conf, reboot.
> 
> 	The kernel boots, but starts spewing 
> 
> 	hda: lost interrupt
> 	hdb: lost interrupt
> 
> 	over and over.

Make sure that you compiled the kernel with the correct console
option; that is, if you are booting from SRM, make sure you answered
the SRM as console question in the affirmative. Vice versa if you
are booting from ARC console.

Or make your kernel a generic one, then it'll figure it out for
itself.

--Jay++

