>an 64 bit OS and found it really was not and found that I
>lost a lot of money invested on that machine.

AXP Linux and Alpha is 64bit, but Gaussian98 isn't really 64bit.
The Alpha/Linux version uses 32-bit integers, so you need to change
the source code for it.

You CAN modify source code to use 64bit integers with ccc and fort for 
AXP/Linux.


>When I run Gaussian98 with an input requirin the direct access exceeding the
>limit of 2GB, the computer reboot after some time leaving no evidence of
>crash.
>Therefore, I think access to memory limit outside of the 32 bit limit may
>cause
>this kind of trouble.
>
>Why on earth the 64 bit Alpha should be limitedto 32 bit on LINUX !?

Please see above.  By the way, which revision of Gaussian98 are you using
on which machine with what distribution/kernel and compilers?
