Dear All.and particularly Iwao,

I am surprized to get comments from many people so quckly..

> AXP Linux and Alpha is 64bit, but Gaussian98 isn't really 64bit.
> The Alpha/Linux version uses 32-bit integers, so you need to change
> the source code for it.
>
> You CAN modify source code to use 64bit integers with ccc and fort for
> AXP/Linux.

I did not check the source codes, but I contacted Gaussian Inc. for my
problems and got an aswer that LINUX Alpha was not a 64 bit OS and
they were trying to persuade Comaq to make it 64 bit.  As a remedy they
suggested to use Tru64 UNIX instead.  I just trusted their answer as the
Gaussian98 developer.  That is all.

If the fault is solely on Gaussian98, I would like to change the source
codes.
Will you teach me where to change?

As to the versions, Gaussian98 is A11 and Redhat7.1 is Kernel 2.4.9-12VT,
both are the latest I believe.

Sincerely,

