On Thu, 18 Apr 2002, YujiMiyahara wrote:
> I did not check the source codes, but I contacted Gaussian Inc. for my
> problems and got an aswer that LINUX Alpha was not a 64 bit OS and
> they were trying to persuade Comaq to make it 64 bit.  As a remedy they
> suggested to use Tru64 UNIX instead.  I just trusted their answer as the
> Gaussian98 developer.  That is all.

then Gaussian Inc. is confused.  alpha linux and tru64 are both fully
64-bit operating systems.  once upon a time, about 6 or 7 years ago, alpha
linux was a 32-bit OS.  but most people had never heard of it then.  for
as long as most people have been using it, alpha linux has always been
64-bit.

on both OSes, "int" types are 32 bits by default.  "long" and "void*" are
both 64 bits however.

