> Redhat 7.2 isn't going to be ported to all the old alphas out there, and
> judging from the posts made to this list about it, I think there is a
> need for a distro that focuses squarely on making the alpha truly what
> it can be.

It wouldn't be that hard to put together an unsupported RedHat Alpha
release using the RPMs in the RedHat Rawhide distribution.  Even though
they never publicly anything after 7.1, they are still building fresh
RPMS in Rawhide for the alpha.  I'm running KDE 3.0 and XFree 4.2 out
of Rawhide on my Alpha.  In the case of KDE and XFree 4.2, these are the
same version of RPMS that are in their x86 7.3 beta release (SkipJack).

The main problem I see is the kernel.  They have not keep that up to
date in Rawhide and many of the patches in the SkipJack kernel do not
have alpha equivalents.  An example is the low latency mods.  I have
built my own 2.4.18 kernel RPMs for the alpha by stripping out most of
the patches from a 2.4.18-xx RedHat kernel source RPM.  But that is
not a substitute for commericial or volunteer kernel hacking efforts
to maintain a properly patched Linux kernel for the alpha.

Bob




