apt-get build-dep <packagename>

	Will get all the dependances needed to build <packagename> and
	install them.

apt-get source	<packagename>

	Will get the source of <packagename> and the compenments needed to build
	a package. You wanna drop in your own source, you are free to do so and
	update the version numbers :-)

concatinating a patch to the existing gz file of patches is the minimum
of effort required to update a package. Then you get to something like X windows
that has a seperate patch tree that is compiled into a single gz when the
package
is built. The later is much more difficult to manage.

dpkg-buildpackage

	Will build the packages. All's left is to sign them and distribute them.

> OpenBSD calls it 'faking' the installation, to make sure it will install
