Port? I object to that. If the damned code was written clean in the first 
place there should be little or nothing to port. That people will only 
bother to do things in 32 bit is their folly. Give it about 2 years, and 
the mainstream will be mostly 64 bit.

It's going to get worse.
  Soon people will be buying Itaniums, Hammers, and the splintering will 
get worse. At least, with Hammer, you can have a chance of running the x86 
stuff, albeit in "legacy 32 bit mode"

>My biggest question was posted to the list to see if there would be
>support for such a distro, focused only on the alpha.  It could be based
>on any number of major distros, just with all the developers poised on
>porting libs, proggies, etc to the alpha.
We are going to have to face that issue really soon if we want to keep 
running modern Linux on Alpha.
  Only reason 7.2 got done is that Compaq needed it to avoid a total panic 
runoff on Alpha.
After that I really don't see the next rev happening.
Guess what? The next Red Hat version (skipjack) is about to come out in 
boxes real soon now.
So that will put Alpha 2 revisions behind. Remember 7.2 is still not out on 
AXP.

>I don't know how long you guys have been waiting on redhat 7.2 for the
