One of the things that this reminds me of is that back in the 90's when you
suggested to anyone of usings Alpha's mainly with NT people would say or you
would read them saying - may as well buy a dual pentium pro or pentium II or
whatever. Maybe now if anyone suggests buying an Itanium then the response
will be buy a dual Hammer system or even single! (It'll be ironic if a
single Hammer outperforms an IA64)
 Still there's no escaping the feeling in the pit of the stomach of what an
Alpha could do at the sort clock rates AMD is talking about for the Hammer
:-(
 Maybe the Alpha was ahead of it's time and I guess there is a glimmer of
hope if Intels markets really start to suffer that they'll resurect it or
bring out some sort of High performance RISC cpu in the future.


