On Fri, 19 Apr 2002, Ted Goodridge, Jr wrote:

>	One thing that struck me about bsd is that the ports system
>allows patches to be applied to stock source to make the package run
>better on a specific os/arch type.

Which is also done in RPM packaging via the %ifarch and %ifnarch 
spec file macros.

For example:

%ifarch alpha
%patch -p0 -b .alpha-bugfix
%endif


>	When we had our suggestion list, one thing I noticed was a lack
>of alpha-specific things in the stock code of packages.  (ie, not using
>the full potential of the alpha in the code.)

If you're aware of alpha patches, or other changes to any package 
in Red Hat Linux that would be beneficial, by all means file a 
bugzilla request for enhancement (RFE).  I generally apply 
enhancements and bugfixes to my packages for alpha/sparc/ppc etc. 
usually within a short amount of time if the stuff looks sane, 
even if it is an architecture we don't officially support.


