> they recompiled with -march=i686 -O9  -fultrafast-random-broken-compile
> r-option ?

I produce Icarus Verilog, and I must say that I agree here. I like
making precompiled binaries, complete with installers, because they
cut down on spurious bug reports. People can download and compile
the source, or they can download and install a conveniently packaged
binary and save us both some trouble:-)

I much appreciate the labor that goes into the RedHat distribution,
or any other of the major distributions that support alpha, and I
would rather see them somehow encouraged to keep it up.
