Because I want linux on my alphas, I started experimenting with Debian on
a ancient PII. The one problem is significant. The kernels that will run
have the 2GB file limit. Now that I've been using kernel 2.4.X, I take
this for granted and the issue is significant.

I agree that it is solid (on a PII anyway), not overly difficult to
upgrade and maintain, if very  annoying to install.

I'm using the machine to do backups. I suppose I don't have to make 
tarballs > 2GB, but life is easier (and backup time shorter) if I can.

