Sorry for the partly off-topic post.  Netscape on RH7.1 has
become so fragile, dumping core at the sight of Java, that an
alternative is becoming desirable.  Mozilla looks like a good
candidate, but it has a few issues I'd like to find solutions to
before switching:

There is this "bookmark list" on the left side, wasting precious
pixels.  I pushed it off the edge, but it seems to want to come
back.  Is there a way to get it to quit coming back?

Mozilla does not honor the xmodmap entry ("add control = Caps_Lock")
I use to make the key to the left of the 'A' do what the key in
that location is supposed to do.  Everything else honors that
additional control key except Acroread and Mozilla.  Is there a
way to get Mozilla to honor the xmodmap entry (or something that
would have the same end result)?  (I have to use the local xmodmap
trick instead of the global keyboard mapping trick, because some
users actually _like_ the Caps Lock key.)

Thanks.

Robert Riches
richesr1@inetarena.com




