I've been playing with my shiny new Oxygen VX1 video card in my
PC164/srm, and find that the X Server installed with RedHat 7.1
is slightly imperfect. I'm getting flashes of video noise during
video activity.

I tried to install the XFree86 4.1.0-15 rpms from the update
directory, but apparently they have the same sparse memory
problem with the glint driver that I encountered with the 3DLabs
card I replaced. I believe this is a known problem.

Next step: the XFree86-4.2 rpms from the rawhide area. Is this
likely to work? Or better yet, what is the upcoming 7.2 for alpha
likely to include?
