I want to see how the new AMD runs, myself. If it works and it's fun to
use, I'd buy one when the price is right. 

Philosophically I'd like to see a clean break from the x86 architecture,
but am continually surpised that x86 can be flogged so hard. I thought
the 486 would be the end of the line.  

A really strong *nux distro, something as slick and fast as Tru64 on
Alpha, plus some great apps for it would be more important to me than
the name on the chip.

Having had noting but good luck with AMD in the past makes me more
willing to take a jump.

my 2 cents.

jn




