Dear Rich Payne


I finally had time to try to change from AlphaBios to the SRM Console. 
It did not work, but at least, following your instructions, I was able 
to go back to the AlphaBios and the machine is running although not 
upgraded...

If you allow me I will try to tell you what I have done and where it 
went wrong. For this I copied the installation instructions on this email:

|======= install.txt from  up1000_srm_5.6_beta.zip  ==========
|
|1) set the firmware configuration jumpers to select
|Recover Firmware (J43) and restart the system; you
|will see the "Don't Panic" summary--read and follow
|the following commands and proceed with the next steps:
|
| 
<Enter>
| 
scan

No problem with this part.

|2) load diagnostics (v1.33 from file 6100391H.rom) from
|floppy and reflash (burn) over the current diagnostics
|(this will be in section 5 on the flash rom map starting
|at sector 8 for a length of 4 sectors):
|
| 
load
| 
floppy
| 
6100391h.rom 

| 
<Enter>
| 
burn 5
| 
<Enter>


Again no problem.

|3) erase alphabios and any other sectors except the
|final sector:
|
| 
erase 8
| 
erase 7
| 
erase 6

No problem

|4) load failsafe recovery (6100411H.rom) from floppy
|at section 6 at sector 12 for a length of 4 sectors);
|it reports itself as Debug Monitor:
|
| 
load
| 
floppy
| 
6100411h.rom
| 
<Enter>
| 
burn 6
| 
<Enter>

Again no problem

|5) load SRM Console (6100501A.rom) from floppy;
|it will go into section 7 at sector 16 for 12 sectors:
|
| 
load
| 
floppy
| 
6100501a.rom
| 
<Enter>
| 
burn 7
| 
<Enter>

First problem! It said there was not enough space. I went back to step 3 
and when I got here it burned the SRM without problem. HOWEVER I am not 
sure I did not erase something I should not because when I went back to 
AlphaBios I had to change from "burn 7" to " burn G" otherwise it said 
there was a mismatch in the sectors. The software for upgrading the Bios 
(The Red console) reported the position of the various components as A, 
B, C, ... and not numbers.



|6) Restore J43 to the Off position, reset the system,
|and verify that Diagnostics 1.33 runs. If instead you
|use the quit command or reset without restoring J43,
|the attempt to load a BIOS image will abort and you
|will return to the Flash menu. After the three rising
|beep tones, you will may see the video BIOS initialization
|messages and then the SRM Console blue screen.

I got here!

|There should be messages about testing the system and memory,
|status for processor 0, and the version of the firmware.

This I did not get. Only a blue screen.

|If you do not see these messages or the command
|prompt (">>>"), type the following:
|
| 
<Enter>
| 
set console graphics
| 
init

I tried this without success. So in the end I flashed the nautilus.rom 
back in the sector G and the Alpha Bios is back and the machine is running.


The graphical description of the BIOS for the SRM looks like

-----------------------------------------------------------
|A|B|B|B|C|E|E|E|E|F|F|F|F|G|G|G|G|G|G|G|G|G|G|G|H|H|H|I|J|
-----------------------------------------------------------

and for the Alpha Bios (9 sectors instead of 11)

-----------------------------------------------------------
|A|B|B|B|C|E|E|E|E|F|F|F|F|G|G|G|G|G|G|G|G|G|H|H|H|H|H|I|J|
-----------------------------------------------------------


where

   A-Unknown
   B-CBOX
   C-Unknown
   D-CBOX
   E-Diagnostics 1.33  (file 6100391h.rom)
   F-Debug Monitor     (file 6100411h.rom)
   G-SRM Console (file 6100501a.rom) (or ARC/NT Bios depending on the
                                      BIOS, file nautilus.rom)
   H-Empty
   I-NVRAM DAta
   J-Diags log


Do you have any idea that might help me? How do I manage to get the >>> 
prompt?


Thanks a lot for your help.

Jorge

