On Fri, Apr 26, 2002 at 07:57:20PM -0500, Ted Goodridge, Jr wrote:
> Whats a specfile?

"specfile" is, in general terms, a set of formal instructions which
tell how to prepare (including possible patching), configure, compile
and _package_ a set of sources into a ready to install rpm binary
archive or archives.

> And where do I find it to help me understand how to
> build this beast born of Mike's hard work?

Inside of your source rpm.  If you "install" it they you will find this
"specfile" in SPECS subdirectory.  But if just want to recompile things
then type 'rpmbuild --rebuild this_package.src.rpm' and, if you have all
pieces required for that installed, what you think that may happen
should indeed happen automagically.

If you will do that with XFree then this will take quite a chunk
of time and a disk space (to be recovered when you are done).
Try first with something small.

   Michal




