> I see you are using a debian kernel for alpha? (or am I wrong?)

You are really wrong and you do not see which kernel I am using.
You only see which kernel was running on a machine when this server
was recompiled and this time it was not me who did it.  As for what
_I_ am using I use the whole range of kernels and those which are
usable on my box I compiled myself. :-)

> where do I get it?

This was one of "rawhide" kernels.  The current one for Alpha there
has a version 2.4.9-31.1 and 2.4.9-31 is currently in updates to
RH 7.1 distribution.  Nothing really stops you from using it with
Debian, of course, as long as "minimal requirements" spelled out
in 'Changes' file of a kernel documentation are satisfied.
Kernels do not depend on a mix of user-space libraries.

   Mcihal




