Hi all,

I have been tourtured by frequent troubles with my Alpha.
Will any one help me out?

I thought LINUX was robust and free from freezes. I thought 
that pure multitasking OS will not stop by failure of one 
process.  My understanding proved to be wrong. My Alpha 
freezes or reboots in calculations requiring long times. What 
is wrong?  Alpha's hard?  LINUX?

I bought the Alpha to use it's 64 bit capability for 
the Gaussian98 program.  I posted here for help on that issue 
previously and got messages from several people.  
Unfortunately, 64bit Gaussian is not realized as yet.  However, 
even for simpler less demanding jobs for Gaussian98 my Alpha 
fails when calculation time gets long.  I have been using 
Gaussian program over the years mainly on Window machines.  
I have experienced lots of troubles with Windows, but 
none with Gaussian on Windows.  At least to me LINUX is 
less reliable than Win2K in long term stability 

Is there any way to diagnose which is the cause of freezing, 
the hardware or LINUX or Gaussian98?  

Thanks in advance.

Yuji Miyahara






