> 
> > Is there anything useful in logs?
> I found messages from the kernel and memory allocation

This is not very illuminating.

There should be file called REPORTING-BUGS on your machine
(try 'locate REPORTING-BUGS') which describes how to decode something
like that and what other information to provide.  Regardless
where you are sending that just a bunch of numbers is in most
circumstances pretty useless.

> Apr 26 08:30:24 vtalpha6s kernel: pc = [buffer_insert_inode_queue+28/80]  ra
> = [__block_commit_write+276/416]  ps = 0000    Not tainted

What kind of distro is that where klogd is mangling logs?  Some
kind of SuSE?  Usually it is to your advantage to run klogd with '-x'
option and decode data with a help of ksymoops.

  Michal




