I'm pretty sure it disregards the registered ram. Though whatever you buy they
first must have EEPROMS so when the machine is first powered up it can figure
out how much ram it (and what kind) has (from SROM, before SRM).

The spec for the micron ram I quoted previously (last month) for an LX has
exactly what it needs.

